# Static site project guidance

Use the existing rootless GptClaw Node/pnpm profile and managed lifecycle.
Read the approved project spec/design/tasks before material product changes.
Preserve unrelated source and Git work; deliver reviewable PRs. Use synthetic data.

This is Next.js static export, not a request-time application server. Edit app/
and public/; lib/site.ts owns the build-time private prefix. Keep navigation and
health working. Server actions, cookies, middleware, runtime image optimization,
ISR and runtime secrets are unsupported. No public or production deployment is
implied. Keep credentials and generated output out of Git.

Use managed rebuild after source edits; it stops this preview before exporting.
Failure leaves it unavailable until repair/rebuild; unrelated projects remain
available. Stop retains source. Never prune shared storage to recover a project.
Read README.md for quality checks, starter adaptation and private URL behavior.
Use gptclawctl deps/toolchain for authorized exact dependency/profile changes.
Install hooks and implicit runtime/tool downloads remain disabled. Preserve the
original catalogue provenance; template upgrades require reviewed source changes.
